00:46:00,000 --> 00:46:06,000
Greyhound is a 2020 American war film directed by Aaron Schneider and
starring Tom Hanks, who also wrote the screenplay.

12
00:50:10,909 --> 00:50:16,909
The film is based on the 1955 novel The Good Shepherd by C.

13
00:54:21,818 --> 00:54:27,818
Forester, and follows a US Navy commander on his first assignment commanding a multi-national escort
destroyer group of four, defending an Allied convoy from U-boats during the Battle of the Atlantic.

14
00:58:32,727 --> 00:58:38,727
The film also stars Stephen Graham, Rob Morgan, and Elisabeth Shue.

15
01:02:43,636 --> 01:02:49,636
Greyhound was initially scheduled for theatrical release in the United
States on June 12, 2020, by Sony Pictures Releasing.

16
01:06:54,545 --> 01:07:00,545
The release was delayed indefinitely and then canceled because of
widespread disruption and shutdowns from the COVID-19 pandemic.

17
01:11:05,454 --> 01:11:11,454
Sony sold the distribution rights to Apple TV+, which
released the film digitally on July 10, 2020.

18
01:15:16,363 --> 01:15:22,363
It received positive reviews from critics, with praise for the action
sequences and effective use of its 90-minute runtime.

19
01:19:27,272 --> 01:19:33,272
At the 93rd Academy Awards, the film earned a nomination for Best Sound.

20
01:23:38,181 --> 01:23:44,181
The film explores themes of submarine, allies, atlantic
ocean, world war ii, based on true story.

21
01:27:49,090 --> 01:27:55,090
The tone is emotional and intense.
